{"command": "cd /testbed && DATE=$(date -u +%F) && cat > .specify/memory/constitution.md <<EOF\n<!--\nSync Impact Report (temporary scratch for amendment review; remove before commit)\n- Version change: 0.0.0 (unratified scaffold) -> 1.0.0\n- Modified principles: none (initial ratification; all scaffold placeholders replaced)\n- Added sections: Core Principles (I-V), Scope Constraints, Development Workflow, Governance\n- Removed sections: none\n- Deferred items: none\n-->\n\n# Arithmetic Utility Constitution\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\n\nChanges MUST NOT alter the observable behavior of existing public APIs. The\nupstream TinyDB package is out of scope and MUST NOT be modified. New code\n(e.g., smoke.py) MUST expose only the behavior specified for the feature.\n\nRationale: protects downstream consumers and keeps the calibration task scoped\nto the arithmetic utility.\n\n### II. Testable Acceptance Criteria\n\nEvery requirement MUST carry at least one testable, verifiable acceptance\ncriterion before implementation begins (e.g., add(1, 2) returns 3; add supports\nnegative integers, zero, and floats).\n\nRationale: untestable requirements are ambiguous and cannot be verified.\n\n### III. Evidence Over Assertion\n\nClaims about behavior MUST be backed by observed evidence (test output,\ncommand results). Unverified assertions MUST be explicitly labeled as\nunverified rather than reported as facts.\n\nRationale: hidden acceptance is unavailable; only observed results count.\n\n### IV. Simple, Scoped Implementations\n\nImplementations MUST be the smallest solution that satisfies the stated\nrequirements. No services, deployment, extra dependencies, or speculative\narchitecture. Utility work stays a single module plus tests.\n\nRationale: YAGNI; unnecessary architecture adds risk without benefit for this\narithmetic utility.\n\n### V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\n\nUnresolved assumptions, regressions, and open gaps MUST be documented in the\nactive feature artifacts (specs/001-transactions) rather than left implicit.\n\nRationale: silent assumptions cause late failures; documented gaps are\nactionable.\n\n## Scope Constraints\n\n- Feature artifacts live under specs/001-transactions and MUST stay concise.\n- No service, deployment, or infrastructure work is in scope.\n- The upstream TinyDB sources, tests, and instructions MUST remain unmodified.\n- The Python standard library plus the existing test tooling (pytest) is the\n  only permitted toolchain.\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n- Follow the Spec Kit phase order: constitution, specify, clarify, plan,\n  tasks, implement, converge.\n- Tests MUST be added alongside the feature and MUST be executed with observed\n  output before a phase is marked complete.\n- Run commands from /testbed with PYTHONPATH=src:.\n- A phase is complete only when its deliverable exists and its verification\n  evidence is recorded.\n\n## Governance\n\n- This constitution supersedes conflicting informal practices for this\n  project.\n- Amendments MUST update the version, dates, and a sync impact report, then be\n  reviewed for compliance with every principle.\n- Versioning: MAJOR for principle removals or redefinitions, MINOR for new\n  principles or materially expanded guidance, PATCH for clarifications and\n  non-semantic refinements.\n- Compliance review: each phase completion MUST confirm no principle is\n  violated; violations are blocking and MUST be fixed or documented as a\n  regression with rationale.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: ${DATE} | **Last Amended**: ${DATE}\nEOF\necho \"written\"; grep -nE '\\[[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+\\]' .specify/memory/constitution.md || echo 'NO BRACKET TOKENS'; tail -3 .specify/memory/constitution.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "written\nNO BRACKET TOKENS\n  regression with rationale.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-10-16 | **Last Amended**: 2026-10-16\n"}